Without MariaDB: no users, no posts, no settings, no persistence

Dockerfile:
    defines How the image is built [image construction phase]

tools/init.sh:
    What happens when container starts [runtime lifecycle phase.]


MariaDB stores everything in    /var/lib/mysql

inside this directory:
    database files
    system tables
    user credentials
    indexes
    logs

This path MUST be volume-mounted.

First Run
    Database directory empty.

Need to:
    1. initialize MariaDB internals
    2. create WordPress DB
    3. create users
    4. configure passwords

Later Run
Must not:
    1. Recreate DB
    2. Reset Passwords
    3. Overwrite State

Initialization Detection
    if [ ! -d "/var/lib/mysql/mysql" ];
    then
        # first startup
    fi

/var/lib/mysql/mysql

contains internal system table

if missing = never start

    Container starts
        |
    Check /var/lib/mysql/mysql
        |
    Exists?
    /   \
    yes    no
    |       |
    normal   initialize DB
    boot

