---

Dockerfile Layer System
    Every Docker instruction creates an immutable filesystem layer.


RUN apt-get update                          creates one layer
RUN apt-get install -y mariadb-server       creates another layer

    Base Image Layer
        ↓
    apt update layer
        ↓
    MariaDB install layer
        ↓
    Copied scripts layer

This is why caching exists.

Before MariaDB can run: system tables must exist.


Initialize using:
    mariadb-install-db --user=mysql --datadir=/var/lib/mysql

this creates:
    mysql.user
    mysql.db
    internal privilege tables

without: MariaDB cannot boot


temporary bootstrap server
- Now you need MariaDB running temporarily.
- Purpose: execute SQL initialization commands.

start temporary server:
    mysqld --skip-networking &


